:: Day3Start [nobr]
<div class="title-screen">
<div class="th">पहला बदलाव</div>
<div class="te">Day 3   Pehla Badlav · First Change</div>

<p class="lede">4:00 AM. Two rooms on opposite sides of Pune, two alarms muffled under two pillows. Arjun in PG Room 12 with Rohit snoring an arm's length away. Kavya in Room 304 with Meera awake against the wall, watching her dress   because Meera is the one person who can't come, and the whole point of today is getting her boyfriend to her.</p>

<p class="lede">Today Arjun and Kavya trade bodies for twelve hours   the first full swap, the one every rehearsal was for. But first each of them has to get out of their room without waking anyone and across the city to a 1,500-year-old cave temple, empty at this hour, before the sky thins.</p>

<p class="lede">You play both threads. The header toggle up top switches whose pre-dawn you're living   and the ritual can't start until they're <i>both</i> at Pataleshwar.</p>

<div class="start-btn">
<<link "4:00 AM   get up">><<goto "Hub">><</link>>
</div>
</div>


:: day3_temple_wait
<<img "pataleshwar_dawn.png" "Pataleshwar, pre-dawn">>
You sit on the cold steps and watch the sky do the thing skies do just before dawn   not lightening exactly, just thinning, like paper held up to a lamp.

<<if $pov is "arjun">>Kavya checks the kumkum tin, the thread, the printed transliteration of the mantra, in that order, twice. "Stop staring at the sky," she says without looking up. "Staring at the sky is not preparation."
<<else>>Arjun's knee is jackhammering. You put a hand on it. It stops for four seconds and starts again. "It's real," you tell him. "I was in Meera's body for ninety seconds. It's real."<</if>>

<<hubreturn "Sit in the circle">>


:: day3_swap
<div class="intimate"><span class="tag">The swap</span>
<<img "pataleshwar_dawn.png" "the kumkum circle">>
<<if $pov is "arjun">>Before the circle, the handover you rehearsed on the phone. You zip the Pulsar key into the left pocket of the riding jacket and pat it once.

"You can actually ride? Properly, not just sit on it?"

<div class="dialogue">"Activa since I was fifteen. Milk runs, gas cylinder runs   the whole family's errand girl. A clutch is just a fourth limb."</div> Kavya's already looking at the bike over your shoulder. <div class="dialogue">"I've wanted to get on a real one for years. Let me have the one good part of today."</div>

"It bucks in first if you drop the clutch. Key's in the jacket   which is about to be your jacket."
<<else>>Before the circle, the handover you rehearsed on the phone. Arjun zips the Pulsar key into the left pocket of the riding jacket and pats it once.

<div class="dialogue">"You can actually ride? Properly, not just sit on it?"</div>

"Activa since I was fifteen. Milk runs, gas cylinder runs   the whole family's errand girl. A clutch is just a fourth limb." You're already looking past him at the bike. "I've wanted to get on a real one for years. Let me have the one good part of today."

<div class="dialogue">"It bucks in first if you drop the clutch. Key's in the jacket   which is about to be your jacket."</div>
<</if>>

<<if $pov is "arjun">>You look at the circle   red powder, a length of string, a printed sheet of Sanskrit   and it looks exactly like what it looks like: two people about to do a craft project and call it a miracle.

"You've actually done this. It actually happened."

<div class="dialogue">"Ninety seconds. Meera and me, night before last, right on this stone. I woke up looking at my own face from the wrong side and I was sick in the bushes. It's real, Arjun. It's real //and// it's insane   both are true, and we don't have time for you to make peace with that."</div>
<<else>>Arjun keeps looking at the circle like it's a card trick he's being slow to catch.

<div class="dialogue">"You've actually done this. It actually happened?"</div>

"Ninety seconds. Meera and me, night before last, right on this stone." You don't dress it up. "I woke up looking at my own face from the wrong side and I was sick in the bushes. It's real. It's also insane. Both, at once. Sit."
<</if>>

You sit cross-legged, knees almost touching, inside a circle of red kumkum drawn on the stone. <<if $pov is "arjun">>Kavya loops the kalava thread around both your right wrists and pulls it taut.<<else>>You loop the kalava thread around both your right wrists   yours and Arjun's   and pull it taut.<</if>>

<<if $pov is "arjun">><div class="dialogue">"Last chance to back out."</div>

"No." The word is immediate. Behind it: Meera. Always Meera.<<else>>You say it out loud, testing whether either of you means it: <div class="dialogue">"Last chance to back out."</div>

Arjun shakes his head. "No." Immediate. Behind it, you both know, is Meera.<</if>>

The chant begins   Kavya leading off the printed sheet, six weeks of Meera's drilling in every vowel, careful and close enough; the other stumbling a half-beat behind, hauled back on line with a sharp tongue-click each time. Two voices, no priest, no witnesses   just what the two of you carried up the hill. They layer anyway. Find rhythm. The dark around the lamp seems to lean in.

Count 50   heartbeat only. Count 80   the thread warms against skin. Count 90   pressure behind the eyes, a headache arriving at light speed.

Count 97   <b>THE WRENCH.</b>

Not physical   essential. Something grabs the substrate of //you// and yanks it through a drain that exists in the cracks between things. A sound like the universe tearing a page.

Black.
</div>
\
<<run setup.setBody("arjun", "kavya")>>\
<<run setup.setBody("kavya", "arjun")>>\
<<run setup.flag("swap_complete")>>\
<<set $swapActive to true>>\
<<run setup.doSwap()>>\
<<run setup.removeItem("bike_keys", "arjun")>>\
<<run setup.addItem("bike_keys", "kavya")>>\
<<run setup.removeItem("redmi_phone", "kavya")>>\
<<run setup.addItem("redmi_phone", "arjun")>>\
<<run setup.stat("rel_arjun_kavya", 3, "arjun")>>\
<<run setup.stat("rel_kavya_arjun", 3, "kavya")>>\
<<run $time.arjun = 330>>\
<<run $time.kavya = 330>>\
<<run $loc.arjun = "hostel_walk_d3">>\
<<run $loc.kavya = "pulsar_ride_d3">>\
<<set $mood.arjun to "on the wrong side of a mirror">>\
<<set $mood.kavya to "admin access after three years of read-only">>

<div class="continue-nav"><<link "Sit up. Look at each other.">><<goto "day3_briefing">><</link>></div>


:: day3_briefing
<div class="intimate"><span class="tag">The handover</span>
<<img "day3_briefing.png" "two strangers wearing familiar faces">>
The wrench recedes. Colour bleeds back into the world. You're sitting in the kumkum circle, breathing like you sprinted a mile, and three feet away your own face is looking back at you wearing an expression you have never once seen from the inside.

<<if $pov is "arjun">>"It worked." Your voice   Kavya's voice, higher, the Tamil under it   comes out in pieces. "It //worked//. That's my face. On you. You're //in// there." You raise a hand and it's small and dusky and ringed and it obeys you. "I said yes but I didn't //believe// it   I thought we'd sit here and nothing would happen and I'd still get to hear about Meera. And instead I'm   am I actually //you// right now? Is this real? This is real?"

<div class="dialogue">"It's real. Now stop hyperventilating   those are my lungs and they're smaller than you're used to."</div>
<<else>>Arjun is coming apart in the best possible way, in your body: hands out in front of him, turning them over, pressing them to his own (your own) face, hair, throat.

<div class="dialogue">"It worked. It //worked//. That's my face on you. Say something, I need to hear my voice from outside   //oh my god//. I said yes but I never believed it. I'm actually   am I actually you? Is this really happening?"</div>

"It's real." Your own voice, an octave lower, steady because one of you has to be   though inside you're screaming too: you have //this// as a body, flat-chested, centre of gravity six inches too high, hands like shovels. "It's real, and you have about fifteen minutes of being useless before we both have to walk out of here. So land the plane."
<</if>>

Grey light is starting to come up behind the caves. The temple's still empty   you have maybe fifteen minutes before the first devotee climbs the steps, and every second of it counts. Then the day.

Kavya   in Arjun's body   goes first, because of course she does. She has an actual list: a folded sheet of ruled paper from the kameez pocket, her half of the day written out in the round hand you're about to have to forge. She presses it into your palm and talks you through it, line by line.

<div class="dialogue">"Ramesh calls you 'didi,' don't flinch. Sign the register slow   my hand is round, yours is block capitals, split the difference. Priya is the danger: planted observer, reads posture. Sit like you're annoyed. Kavya is annoyed by default."</div>

<div class="dialogue">"Bathroom is not optional and it's the squat kind   brace a foot on the door. Wipe front to back, I mean it, a UTI in my body is a war crime. Sneha will quiz you on pathology in the corridor; apoptosis shrinks, necrosis swells, that's all you need. Dupatta lives on the left shoulder. It will not stay. Accept it."</div>

You fold her page into your pocket. Then it's your turn   you've done the same thing, a page torn from a lab notebook, your block capitals, everything she'll need   and you hand it over and hear your own voice aimed back at you.

<div class="dialogue">"Rohit's the sensor   two years living with me, he'll catch any behavioural change. Short answers, shrug, blame no sleep. Do <i>not</i> be brilliant in Krishnan's class. One clever line is a YouTube tutorial; a full optimisation is a knowledge bomb you can't walk back."</div>

<div class="dialogue">"Pooja texts fast and reads everything   three words or nothing. Aai will hear something under the voice, keep the call short. Clutch bites high, bucks once on the first release. Wallet left pocket, ID in the wallet, and the free chai at Raju's is real   take it."</div>

<<if $pov is "arjun">>Then she takes your wrist   her own wrist, small, the silver ring   and holds it until you're looking at your own face gone dead serious.

<div class="dialogue">"One rule above every other one. You do not touch my body. Not curiosity, not 'just to see,' not one second longer in the shower than washing takes. You wash it, you feed it, you put it to bed. That is the entire list of what your hands are allowed to do in there."</div>

<div class="dialogue">"If I come back into it and I //know// you crossed that line   the swaps stop, permanently. Meera loses this. And I will make the rest of your year genuinely unpleasant, and she will hold your Pulsar keys while I do it. Say it back to me."</div>

"I understand. I gave my word to Meera and I'm giving it to you   nothing your body doesn't need. I swear it."

<div class="dialogue">"Good. Same terms the other way; yours is safe with me. Now get up."</div>

Kavya stands   your legs, unfolding to a height she keeps misjudging. "Twelve hours. Back here, 5:30 sharp   that's the clean window and it's the last time I can walk into the hostel without a story. Don't lose my body and I won't lose yours."
<<else>>Then you take his wrist   your own wrist now, thick and strange   and hold it until he's looking at his own face gone hard.

"One rule above every other one. You do not touch my body. Not curiosity, not 'just to see,' not one second longer in the shower than washing takes. Wash it, feed it, put it to bed. That is the entire list of what your hands may do in there."

"If I come back into it and I //know// you crossed that line   the swaps stop, permanently. Meera loses this. And I will make the rest of your year genuinely unpleasant, and Meera will hold your Pulsar keys while I do it. Say it back."

<div class="dialogue">"I understand. I gave my word to Meera, I'm giving it to you   nothing your body doesn't need. I swear it."</div>

"Good. Your body's safe with me   same terms." You stand   Arjun's legs, and the ground arrives later than you expect. "Twelve hours. Back here, 5:30 sharp   any later and I'm signing into the hostel with a lie. Try not to cry with my tear ducts, they file paperwork."
<</if>>

You touch your own borrowed face once, to confirm it's really there, and walk out of the temple in opposite directions.
</div>
\
<<run setup.flag("day3_briefed")>>\
<<run setup.discover("a fifteen-minute crash course in a life", $pov)>>
