:: EV_a3_priya_out
Priya scoops up her laptop and two pathology textbooks at 1:15 and heads for the library, complaining about apoptosis the whole way to the door. It closes. The lock engages.

The room is yours. Meera's already sitting up straighter.

<<hubreturn>>


:: EV_a3_checkin_arjun
<div class="alert-popup swap" style="position:static;max-width:none;margin-bottom:1rem;">📞 Arjun (VIT Ref. Desk)</div>

You call the number. He picks up   your own voice, coming back at you through a phone, wrong and familiar.

<div class="dialogue">"I answered Krishnan's question about red-black tree deletion. Gave a Sedgewick optimisation he hadn't considered. Whole room went silent."</div>

"Too much?"

<div class="dialogue">"Way too much. But Arjun   the //keyboard//. I've written more code today than in three months. I cried. //One// tear. Your tear ducts are bureaucratic."</div>

You tell him about the formalin, about Priya noticing "Kavya" looked relaxed, about washing your hands fourteen times. He tells you the Pulsar is a death machine and he loves it.

For a moment it's just two people laughing down a phone line in each other's voices.

<<run setup.stat("rel_arjun_kavya", 2, "arjun")>>
<<hubreturn>>


