:: EV_a3_aai_call
<div class="alert-popup danger" style="position:static;max-width:none;margin-bottom:1rem;">📞 Aai ❤️</div>

You can't not answer. Arjun always answers his mother.

<div class="dialogue">"Beta, kha liya? ... Sirf dosa? Ande kha, protein chahiye. ... Sunday confirm hai na? Pooja ne bola tu jaldi reply kar raha hai. Kuch hua kya?"<span class="gloss-en">Son, have you eaten? ... Just a dosa? Eat eggs, you need protein. ... Sunday's confirmed, right? Pooja says you're replying fast. Did something happen?</span></div>

"Kuch nahi Aai. Bas class mein free tha."<span class="gloss-en">Nothing, Aai. Just had a free period.</span>

<div class="dialogue">"Hmm. Tera voice thoda alag lag raha hai. Sardi toh nahi lagi?"<span class="gloss-en">Hmm. Your voice sounds a little different. You haven't caught a cold?</span></div>

Same vocal cords. Same pitch. But a mother is hearing something underneath   the cadence, the faintly Tamil syntax you build Hindi sentences with. Mothers are debugging tools, and this one just logged a warning.

"Voice theek hai, Aai. Neend puri nahi hui."<span class="gloss-en">My voice is fine, Aai. Didn't sleep enough.</span>

<<run setup.stat("aai_suspicion", 1, "kavya")>>
<<hubreturn>>


:: EV_a3_papa_call
<div class="alert-popup danger" style="position:static;max-width:none;margin-bottom:1rem;">📞 Papa</div>

Arjun always answers his father too   but for a completely different reason. You pick up on the first ring, the way you've watched him do it, spine straightening on reflex.

No greeting. Papa doesn't greet.

<div class="dialogue">"Internal assessment marks. Pharmacology, DBMS, OS. You were supposed to send them Sunday. Send them tonight."</div>

"Haan, Papa. Aaj bhej dunga."<span class="gloss-en">Yes, Papa. I'll send them today.</span>

<div class="dialogue">"Attendance?"</div>

"Seventy-eight percent." You have no idea. It's a number that sounds survivable.

<div class="dialogue">"Hmm. Krishnan's course is the one that matters. If you're serious about the campus placement, it's not the year to coast. Sunday, one o'clock, Vaishali. Bring a printout of the marks, not a screenshot."</div>

"Theek hai, Papa."<span class="gloss-en">Alright, Papa.</span>

Click. Forty seconds. He didn't ask how you are, didn't hear anything under the voice, didn't notice a single thing   because noticing would require having looked at his son even once in the last five years, and he hasn't.

<div class="thought kavya">Aai clocked something in three sentences. This man wouldn't clock the swap if you told him. That's not a security feature. That's the saddest thing you've learned all day, and you've spent it in someone else's skin.</div>

<<run setup.stat("rel_arjun", 3, "kavya")>>
<<hubreturn>>


