The room is yours. The laptop is yours. Two hours.

<<hubreturn>>


:: EV_a3_swapback_reminder_k
Arjun's phone buzzes. Meera, via the Samsung: //5:30. Pataleshwar. Twelve hours exactly, and it's the last hour Kavya can slip back into the hostel unnoticed. He needs his body and you need yours. And Kavya   thank you. For the CS classes. For all of it.//

You look at the clock in the corner of the borrowed screen. The keyboard under your hands. Soon this stops.

<<hubreturn>>


:: day3_swapback
<div class="intimate"><span class="tag">The swap-back</span>
<<img "pataleshwar_dawn.png" "Pataleshwar, late afternoon">>
The circle again, drawn in the flat gold light of half past five, the courtyard still empty in the lull before evening aarti. The thread. The mantra in reverse   the wrench comes and this time you brace for it, like jumping into cold water the second time.

Black. White. Colours resolving.

<<if $pov is "arjun">>You open your eyes and the first thing you feel is your cock. Right there. The familiar weight you never once appreciated in twenty-one years. Your chest is flat. Your lungs expand fully. You're taller   the temple walls are back at eye level.

And, strangely, a flicker of loss. Kavya's body was terrifying and alien and also a country you'd barely entered, a language you spoke for twelve hours and were just starting to understand.

"Tera dissection class bhayanak hai,"<span class="gloss-en">Your dissection class is horrifying.</span> you tell Kavya, who's patting herself down   face, chest, hips, the body-audit of a woman reclaiming her property.

<div class="dialogue">"Tere Rohit ko control karo. Also your bike's in VIT lot B, keys in your jacket. I didn't scratch it."<span class="gloss-en">Get your Rohit under control.</span></div>
<<else>>You open your eyes and your breasts are BACK   two familiar masses dropping into position, the Clovia underwire clamping down. Twelve hours flat-chested and free, and now the whole production returns.

The world rises. You're looking up at the Nandi statue again. Small again. And between your legs: the absence where a warm, present, slightly ridiculous weight used to be. Not wrong. Familiar. But the familiarity has a new texture now.

"Your laptop is beautiful," you tell Arjun, and the tears come, fast, Kavya's zero-latency system firing. "I wrote two thousand lines of production code. I //coded//, Arjun. On a real keyboard."

<div class="dialogue">"Also your Pulsar is a death machine and I love it."</div>
<</if>>

You both laugh. Real laughter, in your own voices, bouncing off 1,500-year-old stone. Tomorrow you do this again. The thought is terrifying and inevitable in equal measure.
</div>\
<<run setup.setBody("arjun", "arjun")>>\
<<run setup.setBody("kavya", "kavya")>>\
